                                "sense_id": "067c6399-bf3f-32e7-829f-d1631906fcfd",
                                "text": "...what pain that is, I will not temerously judge, but commit it to the goodness of our Iord, whose judgments be very deep and profound;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a2bf41-b1d7-420b-b086-5c6c716dfe7c",
                                "sense_id": "067c6399-bf3f-32e7-829f-d1631906fcfd",
                                "text": "The second, that he swear not temerously or lightly without reverence of God's majesty, but with judgment: that is to say, when necessity constraineth for the glory of God or defence of virtue, at the commandment of a just and lawfully appointed judge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "040e62fd-7fb3-4b3b-8bbf-bc26bc7d149d",
                                "sense_id": "067c6399-bf3f-32e7-829f-d1631906fcfd",
                                "text": "And temerously, his hands went over her, over the salt, compact brilliance of her body."
                            }
                        ]
